    "result_text": "All tests pass and the build is green. Here's a summary of what I implemented.\n\n## Change: optional, region-validated `postcode` on owners\n\nThe feature follows the exact pattern the codebase already uses for optional-but-validated fields (`email`/telephone): a small package-private helper called from the validate step, throwing a checked escalation that a handler turns into a 400.\n\n**Contract (OpenAPI)** \u2014 added `postcode` to the `OwnerFields` schema (`openapi.yml`) as an optional string, so the generated `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` gain the field. No bean-validation pattern was added, so POST and PUT both flow through the same explicit validator and produce an identical 400 shape.\n\n**Persistence** \u2014 added a `postcode` field/column to the `Owner` entity and a `postcode VARCHAR(4)` column to all four schemas (hsqldb \u2014 used by tests \u2014 plus h2, mysql, postgres). MapStruct maps the field by name automatically, so it round-trips through create/response with no mapper changes.\n\n**Validation** \u2014 new `OwnerPostcode` helper:\n- absent (`null`) \u2192 accepted (backward-compatible);\n- present \u2192 must be exactly 4 digits, else 400;\n- if the city has a known region (via the existing `Localities` table: Sydney=NSW, Melbourne=VIC, Brisbane=QLD), the value must fall in that region's range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099), else 400;\n- city with no known region \u2192 any 4-digit postcode accepted.\n\nWired into both `ValidateOwnerFields` (POST) and `ValidateOwner` (PUT); `ApplyOwner` now copies `postcode` on update.\n\n**Error handling** \u2014 new `InvalidPostcodeException` (checked) + `InvalidPostcodeExceptionHandler` (400, body `{\"errors\":[\"postcode\"]}`) + escalation YAML, matching the existing telephone/email handlers.\n\n**Tests** \u2014 the provided `AcceptanceTest` (stores a valid postcode, accepts an owner without one, rejects a malformed one) passes, and the full suite is green:\n\n```\nTests run: 3, Failures: 0, Errors: 0, Skipped: 0\nBUILD SUCCESS\n```\n\nThe out-of-range rejection and unknown-region-accepts-any behavior required by the spec are implemented and consistent with the pinned reference tables in the test base, even though no provided test exercises those two branches directly.",
